ew surrounding  your job status is concerned and that  maybe he would like rush that along  sooner rather than later  and he has pushed back against that  theory right from the get-go dan  he has said numerous times and i believe  that he doesn't care about his his job  status this is really about the short  and the long-term  development and then sustainability of  justin fields  of his career that he's trying to  safeguard the young man's career he  doesn't really care what happens to him  meaning if he gets fired he's going to  do the right thing he's going to do  right by the kid  and  that's  and  look i mean most people feel though and  the whole city of chicago feels at least  just put him in there and quite honestly  you know even being as close as i am to  matt i feel he should put him in there  but he really does want to see what andy  dalton can do he really does feel as  though justin obviously doesn't have  there's something that's not making him  comfortable right now to the point where  he would just throw him in there  especially given the deficiencies that  this offense has  and look i respect the hell out of him  for doing it that way because the the  the scrutiny and the pressure that's  being put on him right now to play that  kid  i mean you know it's unbelievable it's  unbelievable and he won't he won't rush  it until he feels as though that's the  best thing for the kid and the heck with  his own job status and i respect that  great broadcast last night with the guys  we appreciate you joining us as always  and uh have fun uh next week in green  bay  you bet thank you that's louis riddick  former nfl defensive back and uh in the  monday night booth with steve levy and  brian gracie we'll take a break our play  of the day is up next here on the dan  patrick show


